  Dot Popper's copy of Lota 0.3.1's Android host manifest
  (ext/lota/phone/host/android in the gem), which android.yml lays over
  Lota's host in the phone project. Its two changes: Dot Popper decides
  what Back does itself, as Escape (Shell::App), so the meta-data below
  asks SDL to trap Back; and the activity also handles the changes
  Lota's list leaves out: grammatical gender, a SIM (mcc, mnc), a
  touchscreen, and the display's colour mode, each of which would
  otherwise end the game, as SDL can't survive its activity being made
  again. Lota's notes follow.

  A Lota game's manifest, in place of the one fledge build android writes
  (Fledge's lib/fledge/templates/android/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml at
  v0.5.1), whose icon mark Fledge fills here too. It adds what
  love-android's manifest asks of the system for LÖVE's engine: OpenGL ES
  3.0, vibration, a full screen with no title bar, and no restart of the
  activity when the screen turns or a keyboard comes and goes.

  Back reaches the game as the key escape, and then SDL closes the app,
  as in LÖVE. A game that decides what Back does itself adds, inside
  <application>:

    <meta-data android:name="SDL_ENV.SDL_ANDROID_TRAP_BACK_BUTTON" android:value="1" />

  and MainActivity then keeps Android 13 and newer from closing the app
  through predictive back, too.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.VIBRATE" />
    <uses-feature android:glEsVersion="0x00030000" />
    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.touchscreen" android:required="false" />
    <application android:label="@string/app_name"@@ICON@@>
        <meta-data android:name="SDL_ENV.SDL_ANDROID_TRAP_BACK_BUTTON" android:value="1" />
        <activity
            android:name="org.setdef.fledge.host.MainActivity"
            android:theme="@android:style/Theme.NoTitleBar.Fullscreen"
            android:configChanges="orientation|screenSize|smallestScreenSize|screenLayout|keyboard|keyboardHidden|navigation|uiMode|fontScale|fontWeightAdjustment|locale|layoutDirection|assetsPaths|density|grammaticalGender|mcc|mnc|touchscreen|colorMode"
            android:launchMode="singleInstance"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
